# Compose Service Rules

- Give each service a clear stable Compose service key; dependencies should target that key on a shared Docker network.
- Keep environment configuration under `environment` and secrets configurable. Use `$$` when a variable must expand inside a container shell rather than on the host.
- Quote host/container port mappings. Publish only ports needed by the host; container-to-container traffic normally needs no `ports` entry.
- Persist state in a named volume or a documented bind mount. Prefer named volumes for database data unless host-side inspection is a stated use case.
- Mount configuration read-only when the container only needs to read it. Do not mount host directories that are absent or generated implicitly without explaining setup.
- Declare external networks at the top-level `networks` mapping, not under `services`. Add an explicit `name` when it must match a network created by another project.
- Do not use a network merely because a similarly named network exists; ensure the provider and consumer refer to the same actual Docker network.
